// spec: module-system.md §3
// Exactly one real body, inside a package's own lookup scope: the
// facade's `use units;` sees both a sibling file module and a
// subpackage facade for one name. (The top-level file-vs-facade
// collision is pinned by facade_ambiguity; this is the same rule one
// level deeper.) Absent the second body this program is green.
use geom;
fn main() -> i32 {
  printf("{}\n", geom.area());
  return 0;
}
// expect: ambiguous module
// expect: exactly one real body
